WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.571
A fire plan does not put every extinguisher in the
lobby.

2
00:00:03.611 --> 00:00:06.485
It puts one at each point on the escape route.

3
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:14.016
The guardrail map does the same for an agent:

4
00:00:14.056 --> 00:00:18.727
eight hops from the user's question to data
leaving, with a control on each.

5
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:27.535
Input and context checks, the planner, identity,
schema, privilege, the send tool,

6
00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:28.888
and the answer itself.

7
00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.593
You have now attacked and defended each one.

8
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.210
Run it, and the lab prints the same map from its
own code.

9
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.710
When a new tool arrives, place it on the map and
ask: does it bring data in, or let data out?

10
00:00:58.175 --> 00:01:01.468
Fire does not change its route when it sees your
plan.

11
00:01:01.508 --> 00:01:06.035
Attackers do, so review the map every time a tool
or data source is added.

12
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.585
Answer the last question, then claim your
completion badge on the Area page.
